Overview
[b]Mindustry Visual Logic[/b] turns mlog into building blocks: drag blocks to build your logic, then export
it as mlog text you can paste straight into a Mindustry processor.

[ul]
[*]The block library is on the left, grouped by category;
[*]The canvas is on the right; a vertical run of blocks is called a [b]chain[/b];
[*]Blocks can nest: drag other blocks into the nest of a nesting block like If and they become its children;
[*]Every new page comes with a [b]Start[/b] — it is the entry point of the program and does not appear in the palette (it is placed automatically).
[/ul]

[b]Export starts at Start[/b]: only the blocks [b]below[/b] it in the same chain make it into the mlog — the blocks before it
and any other chains on the canvas are not exported. So "a program" is "the run of blocks going down from Start".
Start cannot be copied or deleted (a document has exactly one entry point).

Projects are saved as JSON — it stores "which block is whose child, what value every field holds, and where each chain sits on the canvas",
independent of the Godot version and readable by hand. To export mlog use [code]File → Export to clipboard[/code] (or press [code]F5[/code]).